-- A member has a late loan at their branch when a Loan at the member's branch is due before
-- today. The filter reads a field of the member, `this.branch`.
--
-- `velle compare` from an empty spec (an empty file) to this file prints, under "What that
-- changes", this line among others:
--
--   ### Member
--   - Time passing can now make a Member stop being a MemberAtBranchWithLateLoan.
--
-- That cannot happen. A loan due before today stays due before today on every later day, and
-- time passing moves no loan and no member to another branch. The same condition with the
-- filter comparing a field with `this` itself, `exists (Loan where member == this and dueOn <
-- today)`, does not draw the line.
act Branch { name: text }

act Member {
    name: text
    branch: one Branch
}

act Loan {
    branch: one Branch
    dueOn: Date
}

shape MemberAtBranchWithLateLoan = Member where exists (Loan where branch == this.branch and dueOn < today)
